WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:06.609
How can you measure a country’s power?

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:10.650
I mean its ability to impose its will over
other countries.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:16.250
We could measure their GDP, their economic growth or the size of their army.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.760
But I have another idea.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:25.790
The best way of showing your power is forcing
other countries as large as yours to make

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.870
a big sacrifice.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:34.160
Something that goes against their will but
that they’ll do just because you want them

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.520
to.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.840
Well… this is what Trump is trying to do
with the European Union.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.790
And what is this big sacrifice he wants the
Europeans to make?

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:53.380
Easy: cut their ties with the Islamic Republic
of Iran.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:01:00.220
But… is it really that big of a sacrifice?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.010
And most importantly…

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.270
Can he win this bet?

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:15.990
Well, we’ll answer those questions in this
video.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.759
Iran is a country famous for all of those
independent movies you say you liked but…

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:21.369
actually you haven’t even watched.

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:27.509
But there is something even more important
to Iran’s economy: automobiles.

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:37.329
Yes, my dear viewers, Iran is one of the biggest
car manufacturers in all of the Middle East.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.869
Yes, I know what you’re thinking…

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:40.869
Iran?

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:44.549
That’s a… developing country, isn’t
it?

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:45.549
They are… virtually isolated… aren’t
they?

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:49.159
But surprised as you might be, they even have
their own brands.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:55.289
For example, this car you see here is the
KHODRO SAMAND, a sedan that is sold in Iran,

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:56.939
Azerbaijan, Russia and…

00:01:56.939 --> 00:01:57.939
Venezuela!

00:01:57.939 --> 00:01:59.889
OK, don’t expect anything amazing.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:03.270
The engines are old and the manufacturer has
a lot to improve.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.460
But look, what can you expect for 7000 USD?

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.399
Yes,this is its price.

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:19.819
Can you imagine what would happen if we improved
it a bit

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:20.980
with modern technology?

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:27.500
Such a cheap sedan could sell like crazy in
many developing markets.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.810
And this is why, since 2015, when most of
Iran’s sanctions were lifted, many European

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:37.319
companies started investing in the country.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:43.780
Renault to enter new joint venture in Iran

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:49.930
Peugeot-Citroen back on the road in Iran with
deal to build cars

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.860
But there is way more than cars here!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:58.090
You see, the Iranian stock market has a market
capitalization 3 times bigger than the Egyptian

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.090
one.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.709
And they have all kinds of companies.

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:05.090
Unlike other oil rich countries in the region,
Iran’s economy is surprisingly diversified:

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.819
banks, mining companies and even telecoms.

00:03:08.819 --> 00:03:13.670
And this has attracted other European companies
too.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:19.280
Vodafone marks entry into Iran with HiWEB
partnership

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.370
If this wasn’t enough, Iran has a well educated
population.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:27.690
The literacy rate is way higher than that
of Syria, Iraq and many other neighbouring

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:28.690
countries.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.790
More than 4 million citizens study or have
studied at a University.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:36.549
And this means a well trained workforce that
can work for lower wages.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.939
Add to this the fact that the country has
over 80 million people and you have a great

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:42.269
destination for investments.

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:50.870
Nonetheless, this wave of European money has
just stopped all of a sudden.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:57.189
Trump: US will 'absolutely' sanction European
companies that do business with Iran

00:03:57.189 --> 00:03:58.189
But wait a minute!

00:03:58.189 --> 00:03:59.189
Let’s see…

00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:00.819
Donald Trump is the American president, right?

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:06.670
He can make rules for American companies but…
the European ones?

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.909
How can he impose his rules over countries
he doesn’t govern?

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:15.760
Well, today we will answer these questions
but before we do, let’s take a look back

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.840
at history.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.500
A LEGAL DUEL

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:32.720
In March 2018, ZTE, a Chinese phone manufacturer,
had to pay a 1 billion fine to the US.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.880
Why?

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.570
They imported microchips from America and
sold them to Iran.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:41.500
The White House saw it and said…

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:42.500
(((PRETEND TO BE OFFENDED/PASSIVE AGGRESSIVE)))

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.500
‘Aha!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.500
So… doing business with the baddies, huh?

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.430
So now you gotta choose, you pay a crazy fine
or…

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:52.690
I won’t let you sell your stuff in my country’.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.910
Not selling in America, the World’s richest
country, is just not an option.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:05:00.920
So ZTE was willing to pay anything in order
to stay in the market.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.260
And the same is happening with many other
companies.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:12.570
But as we said, European companies started
doing Business with Iran since 2015.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:18.110
And we aren’t talking about buying oil here,
but investments of all kinds.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:25.560
This is why, as soon as Trump passed new sanctions,
the EU confronted him.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.870
Europe requests exemptions from Trump's Iran
sanctions for energy, aviation and more

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:35.810
Basically, European leaders wrote a letter
to the White House asking America to respect

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.140
their economic interests.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.090
As you know, Trump is no big fan of the European
Union.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.940
So you can imagine his answer.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.260
This is why in August 2018, the European Union
took action.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.150
It was…time… for…

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.210
Regulation 2271/96

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.210
What?

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:55.830
Oh… wait a minute… you don’t know what
regulation 2271/96 is all about?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.710
Oh don’t worry!

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.970
No problem!

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:02.100
That’s what I’m here for!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:08.240
You see, Regulation 2271/96 is something like
a legal shield against trade wars.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.120
For example: let’s say CHEVROLET discovers
that RENAULT has a factory on Iranian soil.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.110
They could take the French company to an American
court that would make them pay a fine.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:23.340
Well… in that very same moment, the European
Union would impose an equivalent fine to Chevrolet.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.990
But this is not the end of the story!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:32.550
Say RENAULT says… ‘oomph…

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.110
I think I’ll leave Iran anyway, there’s
too much trouble here!’

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:38.560
Well… in that case, the European Union could
also fine the company because, technically,

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:42.980
they are complying with Washington’s sanctions.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:52.080
In other words, all the companies doing business
with Iran are in dire straits.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.900
If they stay, Washington will screw them.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:57.300
If they leave, Brussels will screw them.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.330
This is a political duel.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.550
Who is more powerful?

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:07.360
Who do the European companies prefer to be
screwed by?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:12.710
Well… now we’ll see.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.390
REALITY CHECK

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:20.280
I’m sure all of you have made an International
transfer at some point.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:24.050
Let’s say you live in Canada and you need
to get paid by an Australian company.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:28.340
When you do the invoice, you don’t give
your normal bank account, right?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.650
Instead, you give a very long number with
some letters.

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.270
Something like this.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:41.160
IMAGEN DE UN CÓDIGO SWIFT
RZBCCZPPXXX

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:47.110
Well, these letters are the so called SWIFT
code.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.370
The SWIFT system is what we use for international
transfers.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.320
It’s a network that connects all of the
World’s banks.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.150
For years, Iran was disconnected from this
network.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:10.130
This means that even if you wanted to do business
with them… you just couldn’t!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.090
How can you do business with somebody you
can’t transfer money to?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:19.780
Of course, you can send money in a briefcase
but… it’s not very convenient.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:25.220
In 2015, when the nuclear deal was signed,
Iran returned to the SWIFT system.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:29.940
And this was the moment when Iran could go
back to the international business scene.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.290
And now you might wonder…

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.210
Who controls this SWIFT system?

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.470
Well… you guessed it!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.510
A company called SWIFT!!!

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:40.940
Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial
Transactions.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:42.719
And guess where they have their headquarters!

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:43.940
Yeah, you guessed it!

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:44.940
In Brussels, Europe.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.340
So yes, I know what you’re thinking now…
if all the international transactions are

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:54.880
managed in Europe, then America doesn’t
have to do much to avoid business with Iran,

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.040
right?

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.200
Wrong!

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.870
You see, SWIFT is a cooperative society.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:05.320
That means all the important decisions are
made by a board of managers with 25 representatives

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:08.930
from the most important banks.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:14.740
And inside of this board of managers there
are two Americans.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.150
One is from CITY BANK and another is from
J.P. MORGAN.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:25.260
And these two representatives will have to
pay crazy fines if they cannot convince their

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:28.270
colleagues to disconnect Iran from the SWIFT
system.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:31.430
If this happened, Iran would be isolated from
the International market.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.010
If you can’t make transactions, you can’t
do business.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.620
It’s that simple.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:39.440
This is such an important matter that the
European Union is already trying to come up

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.560
with an alternative system for international
transactions.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.980
Something like a modern day barter system.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.030
They call it SPV or Special Purpose Vehicle.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:53.090
The idea is, instead of exchanging goods for
Money, Europe wants to pay with credits over

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:54.090
other goods.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.400
For example, let’s say REPSOL, a Spanish
company, wants to buy oil from Iran.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:07.330
Well, instead of paying with cash, they could
pay with an equivalent sum in machinery.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:14.010
Can something like this work?

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.110
Well, only time can tell.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:20.210
But… let’s assume it does.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:24.880
Let’s say that companies start using this
SPV system to trade with Iran.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.980
Let’s go back to the REPSOL example.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:31.390
This dinosaur juice they just bought has to
arrive somehow, right?

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:34.840
Somebody has to transport it on a tanker to
Barcelona’s harbour.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:35.840
Well…

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:39.440
most of the oil tankers on the planet are
managed by a Danish company called MAERSK.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.900
Yes, I know, Denmark is in Europe.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.029
But… guess what!

00:10:43.029 --> 00:10:46.200
No harbour would accept an oil ship if it’s
not insured.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:51.180
And it turns out most of the insurance companies
that work with oil tankers are American or

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.830
have a lot of interests in America.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:11:02.920
Which explains news like this.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:07.590
Shipping giant Maersk to abandon Iran as threat
of sanctions grows

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:10.270
Other countries like China have already found
alternatives.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:14.230
They have enough at stake to convince them
to do everything they can to keep oil supplies

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.529
coming in from Iran.

00:11:15.529 --> 00:11:17.680
It’s their 6th largest provider.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.029
7% of their dino juice imports come from Tehran.

00:11:21.029 --> 00:11:23.500
But Europe is a different animal.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.910
In their case, Iran isn’t important enough
to risk so much on this.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.490
In other words, if Europe wanted to keep buying
crude oil from Iran… they would have to

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:36.040
find: one, new transport companies, two, new
insurance companies and three, they would

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.070
have to use…….

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.390
BARTERING?

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:46.580
OK, look… just about anything is possible.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:51.571
But so far, it seems that America and Donald
Trump is winning this match against the European

00:11:51.571 --> 00:11:52.571
Union.

00:11:52.571 --> 00:11:54.710
And all of this has many consequences.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:59.330
On a previous video, we talked about what
is happening with the international oil markets.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:03.190
In the following weeks, we will talk about
what could happen to the Iranian regime.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:05.100
Meanwhile, the big question is…

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.940
Can these sanctions end the Iranian regime?

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.560
How much can oil prices go up?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:13.410
You can write me your theories and, in the
following days, we’ll see if they match

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.410
with ours.

